        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "604990c8-ece9-3cdf-87ae-ff07fde4c3ba",
                "word": "jaargetij",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6b0836d8-c74c-4d73-9782-6535c7da564e",
                        "entry_id": "604990c8-ece9-3cdf-87ae-ff07fde4c3ba",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "jaargetijen"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "410475af-fc3b-355b-b1e4-4fd4bb3d141a",
                        "entry_id": "604990c8-ece9-3cdf-87ae-ff07fde4c3ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een jaarlijks terugkerende periode van 3 maanden die vooral op de hogere breedten van de aarde samen gaan met duidelijke verschillende klimatologische periodes"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b938feee-df92-4c3b-ae6d-1238cd302e20",
                                "sense_id": "410475af-fc3b-355b-b1e4-4fd4bb3d141a",
                                "text": "Op vrijdag 14 april opent in het Gemeentemuseum de tentoonstelling ‘Rumoer in de stad - De schilders van Tachtig’. 125 jaar nadat de Nederlandse Impressionisten het straatleven in Amsterdam en Den Haag vastlegden, kon Brobbel in Den Haag maar moeilijk bepalen waar precies de schilders hun ezel destijds hadden opgesteld. „Af en toe heb ik maar gegokt”, zegt hij. Het ‘Gezicht op de nieuwe haven’ van Willem Bastiaan Tholen bood bijvoorbeeld weinig aanknopingspunten. Hoe anders was dat met ‘Gezicht op de Keizersgracht’ van Breitner. Het belangrijkste verschil in het stadsgezicht lijkt hier het jaargetij."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "23e0478e-6750-45f1-bf03-7cbfd07c19a0",
                                "sense_id": "410475af-fc3b-355b-b1e4-4fd4bb3d141a",
                                "text": "Geen beter jaargetij om de mooiste bloemen in huis te halen dan de herfst. De werkstukken van vijf bloemisten die het omfietsen waard zijn, omdat ze toppers zijn in hun vak."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "87fbc7dc-1a16-3d3b-8051-c92187f9a4b9",
                        "entry_id": "604990c8-ece9-3cdf-87ae-ff07fde4c3ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "jaarmis"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "07a33fd9-7531-4d45-9196-aea69c3c210f",
                        "source_entry_id": "604990c8-ece9-3cdf-87ae-ff07fde4c3ba",
                        "source_sense_id": "410475af-fc3b-355b-b1e4-4fd4bb3d141a",
                        "source_sense_description": "(meteorologie) een jaarlijks terugkerende periode van 3 maanden die vooral op de hogere breedten van de aarde samen gaan met duidelijke verschillende klimatologische periodes",
                        "target_lang_word": "season",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "season",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ccecbca2-8937-3e38-8c33-dbba5f4d33c4",
                                        "entry_id": "555294d2-354b-3276-95e4-9f582dd64609",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Each of the four divisions of a year: spring, summer, autumn (fall) and winter"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c8f4173-ab85-4104-a0c0-bc5b6a5273f0",
                                                "sense_id": "ccecbca2-8937-3e38-8c33-dbba5f4d33c4",
                                                "text": "We had joy, we had fun, we had seasons in the sun, / But the wine and the song, / like the seasons, have all gone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "081eedad-cbf0-4738-86fd-1d7c465d7be8",
                                                "sense_id": "ccecbca2-8937-3e38-8c33-dbba5f4d33c4",
                                                "text": "we saw, in six days' traveling, the several seasons of the year in their beauty and perfection"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2986818a-0dd5-3309-98c3-e5712c1f4e13",
                                        "entry_id": "555294d2-354b-3276-95e4-9f582dd64609",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A period of the year when something particular happens."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17c05863-b336-4139-9881-c9963363a67d",
                                                "sense_id": "2986818a-0dd5-3309-98c3-e5712c1f4e13",
                                                "text": "the rainy season"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4772519-f1d1-423f-8bac-6fbbe2bf0989",
                                                "sense_id": "2986818a-0dd5-3309-98c3-e5712c1f4e13",
                                                "text": "the football season"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "267c9a8f-a0a2-4982-b152-5d8534bd3fb0",
                                                "sense_id": "2986818a-0dd5-3309-98c3-e5712c1f4e13",
                                                "text": "mating season"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d113cada-f177-4f4f-9132-bc8e8db1b23b",
                                                "sense_id": "2986818a-0dd5-3309-98c3-e5712c1f4e13",
                                                "text": "Then there came a reg'lar terror of a sou'wester same as you don't get one summer in a thousand, and blowed the shanty flat and ripped about half of the weir poles out of the sand. We spent consider'ble money getting 'em reset, and then a swordfish got into the pound and tore the nets all to slathers, right in the middle of the squiteague season."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e44c3a0-de79-470d-b287-32673600af95",
                                                "sense_id": "2986818a-0dd5-3309-98c3-e5712c1f4e13",
                                                "text": "Curry, a four-time NBA champion with the Warriors, played for the Wildcats for three seasons between 2006 and 2009, where he was twice named conference player of the year. […] Curry has been named NBA regular season MVP twice and is an 11-time All Star."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb7d6785-c708-37b4-b90b-aaa02bc3306e",
                                        "entry_id": "555294d2-354b-3276-95e4-9f582dd64609",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A period of the year in which a place is most busy or frequented for business, amusement, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6c7ac28-571c-4964-b3db-84ee7dd38fe7",
                                                "sense_id": "cb7d6785-c708-37b4-b90b-aaa02bc3306e",
                                                "text": "He seldom was seen in the office himself, but occasionally a paragraph in the paper recorded that his yacht had touched at Mentone and that he had been seen at the Monte Carlo tables, or that he was expected in Leicestershire for the season."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a743b1f8-2483-35a0-a66b-d820ec8a5023",
                                        "entry_id": "555294d2-354b-3276-95e4-9f582dd64609",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The period over which a series of Test matches are played."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e77a1a01-29fa-324a-a495-26ead2d28797",
                                        "entry_id": "555294d2-354b-3276-95e4-9f582dd64609",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That which gives relish; seasoning."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d908c28d-0d83-4022-8b50-33e9b6c3d138",
                                                "sense_id": "e77a1a01-29fa-324a-a495-26ead2d28797",
                                                "text": "O! she is fallen\nInto a pit of ink, that the wide sea\nHath drops too few to wash her clean again,\nAnd salt too little which may season give\nTo her foul-tainted flesh."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95583482-c387-48b3-bfeb-bbbeb048f866",
                                                "sense_id": "e77a1a01-29fa-324a-a495-26ead2d28797",
                                                "text": "You lack the season of all natures, sleep."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c367bddf-0226-320d-8cae-c8c2289cb555",
                                        "entry_id": "555294d2-354b-3276-95e4-9f582dd64609",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A group of episodes of a television or radio program broadcast in regular intervals with a long break between each group, usually with one year between the beginning of each."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "Canada",
                                            "US"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a91934d-68d9-4ec8-bc2b-eb07bb6c84ee",
                                                "sense_id": "c367bddf-0226-320d-8cae-c8c2289cb555",
                                                "text": "The third season of Robot Chicken aired from 2007 to 2008."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "104bbe53-9ba5-486e-8179-13c5820718cb",
                                                "sense_id": "c367bddf-0226-320d-8cae-c8c2289cb555",
                                                "text": "Or - is she Erin Gray in the second season of Buck Rogers beautiful?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "81bfd35b-a1c2-3c77-939f-b3616c15c79c",
                                        "entry_id": "555294d2-354b-3276-95e4-9f582dd64609",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An extended, undefined period of time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae6d1ad7-39eb-4b22-b3d7-08ced0e8da35",
                                                "sense_id": "81bfd35b-a1c2-3c77-939f-b3616c15c79c",
                                                "text": "It was the Winter wilde.\nWhile the Heav’n-born-childe,\nAll meanly wrapt in the rude manger lies:\nNature in aw to him\nHad doff't her gawdy trim,\nWith her great Maſter ſo to ſympathize:\nIt was no ſeaſon then for her\nTo wanton with the Sun her luſty Paramour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dde4c5fc-6867-4392-bd86-42c004eae72b",
                                                "sense_id": "81bfd35b-a1c2-3c77-939f-b3616c15c79c",
                                                "text": "So it is in a person when a breach hath been made upon his conscience, quiet, perhaps credit, by his lust, in some eruption of actual sin; — carefulness, indignation, desire, fear, revenge are all set on work about it and against it, and lust is quiet for a season, being run down before them; but when the hurry is over and the inquest is past, the thief appears again alive, and is as busy as ever at his work."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecda12fa-2f3c-4b71-832f-b7658b9ec877",
                                                "sense_id": "81bfd35b-a1c2-3c77-939f-b3616c15c79c",
                                                "text": "A season of great doubt fell upon her soul."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b614e989-b05c-3324-a2c2-365dd10db5c8",
                                        "entry_id": "555294d2-354b-3276-95e4-9f582dd64609",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A period of time in one’s life characterized by a particular emotion of situation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e609830b-4fdb-4e72-aa77-b61b8e624f59",
                                                "sense_id": "b614e989-b05c-3324-a2c2-365dd10db5c8",
                                                "text": "a season of faithlessness"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a810550c-1d09-376b-a77b-a14c8f7f232e",
                                        "entry_id": "555294d2-354b-3276-95e4-9f582dd64609",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The full set of downloadable content for a game, which can be purchased with a season pass."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a4a4c5c3-68ec-3c78-8272-bcca3bb66a12",
                                        "entry_id": "555294d2-354b-3276-95e4-9f582dd64609",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fixed period of time in a massively multiplayer online game in which new content (themes, rules, modes, etc.) becomes available, sometimes replacing earlier content."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "season",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "656efc08-d5de-3cc0-9025-2b12ef5a5c2b",
                                        "entry_id": "03a04010-143e-3705-8041-88ac63d8de42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To habituate, accustom, or inure (someone or something) to a particular use, purpose, or circumstance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a29f3206-ef57-4f83-92b4-bcc5b7ec6862",
                                                "sense_id": "656efc08-d5de-3cc0-9025-2b12ef5a5c2b",
                                                "text": "to season oneself to a climate"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "abc58958-7bde-3fc3-b305-cc55e5a81d70",
                                        "entry_id": "03a04010-143e-3705-8041-88ac63d8de42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To prepare by drying or hardening, or removal of natural juices."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6ca4409-3b16-4b67-a485-20b04c8431b0",
                                                "sense_id": "abc58958-7bde-3fc3-b305-cc55e5a81d70",
                                                "text": "The timber needs to be seasoned."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5382e6ea-9725-33f1-97d3-b22d27877d58",
                                        "entry_id": "03a04010-143e-3705-8041-88ac63d8de42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To become mature; to grow fit for use; to become adapted to a climate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a048d4d6-7a10-3322-9320-4d39908190ab",
                                        "entry_id": "03a04010-143e-3705-8041-88ac63d8de42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To become dry and hard, by the escape of the natural juices, or by being penetrated with other substance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "309314f7-3c28-4902-a50c-b2abf001d250",
                                                "sense_id": "a048d4d6-7a10-3322-9320-4d39908190ab",
                                                "text": "The wood has seasoned in the sun."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f9f0c262-26f8-3ada-acb2-b97e17cb7197",
                                        "entry_id": "03a04010-143e-3705-8041-88ac63d8de42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To mingle: to moderate, temper, or qualify by admixture."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a3ac067-c63b-3851-bab2-7d8b8a9b7d86",
                                        "entry_id": "03a04010-143e-3705-8041-88ac63d8de42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To impregnate (literally or figuratively)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38835c4e-b845-40c0-9013-e2da09220c0f",
                                                "sense_id": "1a3ac067-c63b-3851-bab2-7d8b8a9b7d86",
                                                "text": "When the male hath once ſeaſoned the female, he neuer after toucheth her."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae86f82b-511f-4659-9ff6-d466b331e70a",
                                                "sense_id": "1a3ac067-c63b-3851-bab2-7d8b8a9b7d86",
                                                "text": "For this prince[…]would not ſuffer the Buls to come unto the Kine and ſeaſon them, before they were both foure yeares old."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1535ecd1-83ee-4977-be51-fdd040fb7479",
                                                "sense_id": "1a3ac067-c63b-3851-bab2-7d8b8a9b7d86",
                                                "text": "If you had seasoned me with that philosophy, which formeth the mind to ratiocination, and insensibly accustoms it to be satisfied with nothing but solid reasons, if you had given me those excellent precepts and doctrines, which raise the foul above the assaults of fortune, and reduce her to an unshakeable and always equal temper, and permit her not to be lifted up b prosperity, nor debased by adversity, if you had taken care to give me the knowledge of what we are, and what are the first principles of things, and had assisted me in forming in my mind a fit idea of the greatness of the universe, and of the admirable order and motion of the parts thereof, if, I say, you had instilled into me this kind of philosophy, I should think myself incomparably more obliged to you than Alexander was to his Aristotle"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e7950dc-9c46-4a3b-8855-bc2c13a4da30",
                                                "sense_id": "1a3ac067-c63b-3851-bab2-7d8b8a9b7d86",
                                                "text": "In minds, not seasoned and impregnated with the due apprehension of those ends, that conduce to ease and security, there is usually a tempestuous discontent, that raises unruly ferments; an unkind gale, by whose resistless powers, the port is overreached."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
